      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T09:09:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This would also cancel other requests using other networks for the same service type; meaning you can\u0027t discover one service type on 2 networks (IIUC this comes from a limitation where you can\u0027t discover one service type with 2 different MdnsSearchOptions ?).\n\nThinking about it I think MdnsServiceTypeClient needs to be Network-specific, e.g. have Network in the constructor. Otherwise the instanceNameToResponse cache would be incorrect too: the service attributes may be different on different networks, so there needs to be a different instance of the cache.\n\nSo maybe you\u0027d need something like `Map\u003cString, Map\u003cNetwork, MdnsServiceTypeClient\u003e\u003e serviceTypeClients` in MdnsDiscoveryManager, or `Map\u003cPair\u003cString, Network\u003e, MdnsServiceTypeClient\u003e`.",
      "revId": "dd9e962dabd092a0ddb657bc391d1f8c06333828",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
